From d8917c3144b076d89a5afa280433952cffae3fc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:04:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 148/158] server: Report directory changes as they happen on
 macOS, and in subdirectories.

Watched directories were only rescanned every 50 ms, so a program that
changed a directory and asked at once was told nothing had changed, and a
recursive watch never saw its subdirectories.

The kernel now reports a watched directory whose entries were added,
removed or renamed (EVFILT_VNODE in the main loop's kqueue), which runs
the scan before the requests that arrived with it. A recursive watch
follows subdirectories, within limits on depth, entries and open files,
and reports names relative to the watched directory. The 50 ms poll stays
for changes to the files themselves, which the kernel does not report on
a directory.

Fixes all 6 failures in ntdll:change and all 10 in kernel32:change.
